WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.249
Find Demo Operator Zero One to review the
earnings generated from saved production.

2
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.581
Add an advance of four hundred rupees, with a
short description, and save it.

3
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.553
Recovery now includes the advance, reducing net
pay.

4
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.373
You can also record a deduction.

5
00:00:35.613 --> 00:00:38.805
Select Other as the reason for this
demonstration.

6
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.697
Enter fifty rupees.

7
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.307
Add a short note, then record the deduction.

8
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.562
Net pay now includes both recoveries.

9
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:15.194
Open How Pay Is Calculated for a summary of
piece rate earnings, salaries and advance
recovery.

10
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.738
Choose Mark Paid, then confirm the payment.

11
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.219
Record three thousand three hundred and ninety
rupees as paid.

12
00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:32.171
This does not send money.

13
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.879
Open Payroll Records and find the demo worker
for the pay period.

14
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.984
Expand the payment to see the loom,

15
00:01:53.104 --> 00:01:54.128
costing,

16
00:01:54.248 --> 00:01:57.564
rate and production quantity behind these
earnings.

17
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.809
Switch to the Machines view to summarize
production and worker cost by loom.

18
00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.804
Download the C S V for spreadsheet analysis, or
the P D F for a shareable payroll report.
